## Examples

### Example 1: "Update Bhishma to check for X"
```
→ No local qualifier
→ Apply to GLOBAL (~/.cursor/agents/bhishma.md)
→ All repos get the update
```

### Example 2: "For moby only, Bhishma should also check payment flows"
```
→ "For moby only" = local qualifier
→ Create /Users/uday.jadhav/dev/moby/.cursor/agents/bhishma.md
→ Only moby gets this behavior
→ Other repos use global bhishma
```

### Example 3: "Remove the moby-specific Bhishma rule"
```
→ Delete moby/.cursor/agents/bhishma.md
→ Moby now uses global bhishma
```

---

## Verification

To check what version a repo uses:
```bash
# Check local
ls <repo>/.cursor/agents/

# Check global
ls ~/.cursor/agents/

# Local exists? → Using local
# Local doesn't exist? → Using global
```
